---
id: org.dxos.plugin.space
name: SpacePlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Core workspace container plugin for `DXOS` Composer — creates, manages, and shares collaborative spaces with full membership control, object lifecycle management, schema registration, and navigation.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`    |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`   |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`          |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`    |

## Types

```mdl
type SpaceForm
  fields:
    name?: string               # display name for the space
    icon?: string               # phosphor icon identifier
    hue?: string                # colour token
    edgeReplication?: boolean   # enable EDGE-based replication
    origin?: string             # overrides the invoker's write origin (user | system | unknown)
```

```mdl
type SpacePluginOptions
  fields:
    shareableLinkOrigin?: string  # base URL used for invitation and object copy-links
    invitationPath?: string       # path appended to origin; default '/'
    invitationProp?: string       # query param name for the invitation code
    observability?: boolean       # emit observability events
```

```mdl
type ObjectViewerProps
  desc: One session's view of an object; a session is a tab or app instance of a peer.
  fields:
    lastSeen: number            # unix timestamp of last observation
    movedAt: number             # when the session opened the object, came back to it, or moved its anchor there
    currentlyAttended: boolean  # true if the session is currently viewing this object
    location?: PeerLocation     # the session's selection and top of view in the object, while its deck holds it
    device?: SessionDevice      # the device the session runs on
```

```mdl
type PeerDeck
  desc: A session's deck in one space, as its viewing message reports it.
  fields:
    planks: string[]            # graph paths of the deck's planks in that space, in order
    front?: string              # the plank the deck is scrolled to, when it is in that space
```

```mdl
type SessionDevice
  desc: The device a session runs on, from its HALO device profile; the receiver names it.
  fields:
    label?: string              # a label someone gave the device
    platform?: string           # the browser, or App for the native and mobile apps
    os?: string
    kind?: browser | native | mobile | agent | unknown
```

```mdl
type FollowTarget
  desc: The peer a session follows, or one session of theirs.
  fields:
    spaceId: SpaceId
    identityKey: IdentityKeyHex
    sessionId?: SessionId       # follow this session; otherwise the peer's most recently moved session
```

```mdl
type PluginState
  fields:
    viewersByObject: Record<EID, Record<IdentityKeyHex, Record<SessionId, ObjectViewerProps>>>
    peerDecks: Record<SpaceId, Record<IdentityKeyHex, Record<SessionId, PeerDeck>>>  # each session's last reported deck
    spaceNames: Record<string, string>  # cached names for closed/loading spaces
    sdkMigrationRunning: Record<string, boolean>
    navigableCollections: boolean
    enabledEdgeReplication: boolean
    showSessions?: boolean      # presence lists show a row per session; kept per device
    following?: FollowTarget & { paused?: boolean }  # ephemeral; paused while the leader views something this session cannot open
```

## Components

```mdl
component CollectionArticle
  desc: Main article view for a Collection — renders its child objects as an ordered list, supports drag-reorder and per-item actions.
  props:
    subject: Collection
  state:
    selected?: Obj.Unknown
  actions:
    addObject(object: Obj.Unknown)
    removeObject(object: Obj.Unknown)
    reorder(from: number, to: number)
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────┐
    │  [toolbar]              │
    ├─────────────────────────┤
    │  object row             │
    │  object row             │
    │  object row  …          │
    └─────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component CollectionSection
  desc: Compact list of objects belonging to a collection, used inside sidebars and companion panels.
  props:
    collection: Collection
  state:
    expanded: boolean
  actions:
    toggleExpand()
```

```mdl
component RecordArticle
  desc: Schema-driven form/detail view for a single ECHO object rendered in an article slot.
  props:
    subject: Obj.Unknown
  actions:
    save()
    discard()
```

```mdl
component RelatedArticle
  desc: Companion panel listing objects semantically related to the current subject via ECHO relations.
  props:
    subject: Obj.Unknown
  state:
    relations: Obj.Unknown[]
```

```mdl
component ObjectFormDialog
  desc: Modal dialog that lets the user pick a target and a schema type and fill in a new ECHO object. In `live` mode the object is added to the database before the form opens and removed again on dismissal.
  props:
    target: Database | Collection
    mode?: 'draft' | 'live'
    views?: boolean
    typename?: string
    schema?: Schema
    defaults?: Record<string, any>
    navigable?: boolean
  actions:
    confirm(data: Record<string, any>)
    cancel()
```

```mdl
component CreateSpaceDialog
  desc: Modal dialog for creating a new space with name, icon, colour, and replication options.
  actions:
    confirm(form: SpaceForm)
    cancel()
```

```mdl
component ImportSpaceDialog
  desc: Dialog that accepts a space archive file and imports it as a new space.
  actions:
    confirm(archive: { filename: string; contents: Uint8Array })
    cancel()
```

```mdl
component JoinDialog
  desc: Dialog that accepts an invitation code and joins the corresponding space.
  props:
    invitationCode?: string
  actions:
    join(code: string)
    cancel()
```

```mdl
component MembersContainer
  desc: Panel showing all members of a space with their presence status and role; allows managing invitations.
  props:
    space: Space
```

```mdl
component SpaceSettingsContainer
  desc: Settings panel for a single space — name, icon, colour, replication toggle, and member management.
  props:
    space: Space
```

```mdl
component SchemaContainer
  desc: Browsable table of all registered ECHO schemas in the current space; allows adding new schemas.
  props:
    db: Database
```

```mdl
component ViewEditor
  desc: Interactive editor for a View — reorder, add, and remove fields; configure field display settings.
  props:
    view: View
```

```mdl
component SpacePresence
  desc: Avatar cluster indicating which peers are currently attending the active object/space.
  props:
    spaceId?: SpaceId
    presenceKey?: EID   # the object's EID, or the space's own EID for a space-level view
```

```mdl
component SyncStatus
  desc: Icon/indicator reflecting the CRDT sync health of the active space.
  props:
    space: Space
```

## Operations

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.Create
  desc: Creates a new space with the given display properties.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.create
  input:
    name?: string
    icon?: string
    hue?: string
    edgeReplication?: boolean
  output: { id: string; subject: string[]; space: Space }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.Join
  desc: Joins an existing space by resolving and accepting an invitation code.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.join
  input:
    invitationCode?: string
  output: void
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.Open
  desc: Navigates the layout to the given space.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.open
  input:
    space: Space
  output: void
  effects: [layout:navigate]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.Close
  desc: Removes the space from the active navigation context.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.close
  input:
    space: Space
  output: void
  effects: [layout:navigate]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.Share
  desc: Creates an invitation observable for sharing a space; supports single-use and multi-use codes.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.share
  input:
    space: Space
    type: Invitation.Type
    authMethod: Invitation.AuthMethod
    multiUse: boolean
    target?: string
  output: CancellableInvitationObservable
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.Rename
  desc: Opens a rename popover for the given space.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.rename
  input:
    space: Space
    caller?: string
  output: void
  effects: [layout:dialog]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.AddObject
  desc: Adds an existing ECHO object to a database or collection and optionally navigates to it.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject
  input:
    object: Obj.Unknown
    target: Database | Collection
    hidden?: boolean
    targetNodeId?: string
  output: { id: string; subject: string[]; object: Obj.Unknown }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.RemoveObjects
  desc: Removes one or more objects from a collection; returns undo data.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects
  input:
    objects: Obj.Unknown[]
    target?: Collection
  output: { objects: Obj.Unknown[]; parentCollection: Collection; indices: number[]; wasActive: string[] }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.RestoreObjects
  desc: Restores previously removed objects to their collection (inverse of RemoveObjects).
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.restoreObjects
  input:
    objects: Obj.Unknown[]
    parentCollection: Collection
    indices: number[]
    wasActive: string[]
  output: void
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.AddSchema
  desc: Registers a new schema type in the space database; optionally makes it visible in the type picker.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.addType
  input:
    db: Database
    name?: string
    typename?: string
    version?: string
    schema: Schema.AnyNoContext
    show?: boolean
  output: { id: string; object: Type.PersistentType; schema: Type.RuntimeType }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.AddRelation
  desc: Creates a typed relation between two ECHO objects.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.addRelation
  input:
    db: Database
    schema: Schema.AnyNoContext
    source: Obj.Unknown
    target: Obj.Unknown
    fields?: Record<string, any>
  output: { relation: any }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.DeleteField
  desc: Removes a field from a View; returns undo data.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.deleteField
  input:
    view: View
    fieldId: string
  output: { field: View.FieldSchema; props: any; index: number }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.RestoreField
  desc: Restores a deleted field to a View at its original index (inverse of DeleteField).
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.restoreField
  input:
    view: View
    field: View.FieldSchema
    props: any
    index: number
  output: void
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.ImportSpace
  desc: Imports a binary space archive as a brand-new space.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.import
  input:
    archive: { filename: string; contents: Uint8Array }
    tags?: string[]
  output: { space: Space }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.ExportSpace
  desc: Serialises a space to an archive and triggers a browser download.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.export
  input:
    space: Space
    format: SpaceArchive.Format
  output: void
  effects: [fs:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.Snapshot
  desc: Captures a point-in-time snapshot of a database or filtered query as a Blob.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.snapshot
  input:
    db: Database
    query?: QueryAST.Query
  output: { snapshot: Blob }
  effects: [echo:read]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.Migrate
  desc: Runs registered migrations against a space to bring it to the current schema version.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.migrate
  input:
    space: Space
    version?: string
  output: boolean               # true if any migration ran
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.Reset
  desc: |
    Permanently deletes all objects and truncates feeds in a space via a new epoch.
    This operation is unrecoverable.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.removeAllObjects
  input:
    space: Space
  output: void
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SpaceOperation.GetShareLink
  desc: Constructs a shareable URL for a space or specific object; optionally copies it to the clipboard.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.getShareLink
  input:
    space: Space
    target?: string
    copyToClipboard?: boolean
  output: string                # fully-qualified URL
  effects: [clipboard]
```

```mdl
op CollectionOperation.Create
  desc: Creates a new Collection object in the active space.
  key: org.dxos.operation.space.createCollection
  input:
    name?: string
  output: { object: Collection }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Space Lifecycle

  req F-1.1: User can create a new space via op:SpaceOperation.Create; the space appears in the navigation graph.
  req F-1.2: User can join a space via op:SpaceOperation.Join with an invitation code.
  req F-1.3: User can close/open spaces; closed spaces remain listed with their cached name.
  req F-1.4:
    when: user triggers op:SpaceOperation.Reset
    then: all objects are deleted and a new epoch is created; the operation is unrecoverable
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Membership and Sharing

  req F-2.1:
    when: user triggers op:SpaceOperation.Share
    then: an invitation observable is created; the invitation URL uses the configured shareableLinkOrigin

  req F-2.2: MembersContainer shows all current members with their presence status.
  req F-2.3: User can generate single-use or multi-use invitation links.
  req F-2.4: User can get a direct shareable link to a space or object via op:SpaceOperation.GetShareLink.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Object Lifecycle

  req F-3.1:
    when: user opens the create-object dialog
    then: all registered schema types are shown for selection

  req F-3.2: op:SpaceOperation.AddObject adds an object to a collection and fires navigation if navigable.
  req F-3.3: op:SpaceOperation.RemoveObjects records undo data; op:SpaceOperation.RestoreObjects reverts the removal.
  req F-3.4: op:SpaceOperation.DuplicateObject creates a shallow copy of an object in the same target.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Schema Registry

  req F-4.1:
    when: a plugin registers a schema via AppPlugin.addSchemaModule
    then: the type is available globally across all spaces

  req F-4.2:
    when: user triggers op:SpaceOperation.AddSchema
    then: a StoredSchema entry is persisted in the space database

  req F-4.3: SchemaContainer lists all schemas in the active space; user can add a new user-defined schema.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Collections

  req F-5.1: A Collection is an ordered list of references to ECHO objects.
  req F-5.2: CollectionArticle renders collection contents with drag-to-reorder support.
  req F-5.3: op:CollectionOperation.Create creates an empty Collection in the active space.
  req F-5.4: An object's collection ancestry is its canonical location: `resolveCollectionObjectPath`
             walks the space's collection tree to the root collection and yields
             `content/collections/<ancestors…>/<objectId>`. Both URL resolution (the `object` url key)
             and the plugin's NavigationTargetResolver answer with it, so a link to an object lands
             where the nav tree shows it.
  req F-5.5: The plugin's NavigationTargetResolver offers the collection path first, then the type-section
             path for types whose graph extension declares a static section (derived from the builder's
             url bindings — see `type-section-path.ts` — so no per-plugin wiring), and the database path
             (`system/database/<type>/<objectId>`) last, declared via `position: Position.last` — every
             object has the latter, but it names a hidden node, so it is only used for objects the tree
             shows nowhere else.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Persistence and Migrations

  req F-6.1:
    when: client emits SetupMigration
    then: all registered migrations run against every space

  req F-6.2:
    when: user triggers op:SpaceOperation.Migrate
    then: the space is migrated to the specified (or latest) version; returns true if work was done

  req F-6.3: op:SpaceOperation.ExportSpace serialises a space as a binary archive for backup.
  req F-6.4: op:SpaceOperation.ImportSpace restores an archive as a new space with optional tags.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: View and Field Editing

  req F-7.1: op:SpaceOperation.DeleteField removes a field from a View and returns full undo state.
  req F-7.2: op:SpaceOperation.RestoreField reinstates a deleted field at its original position.
  req F-7.3: ViewEditor provides an interactive UI for reordering and configuring View fields.
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Presence and Sync Status

  req F-8.1: SpacePresence tracks which peers are viewing which objects via the attention system.
  req F-8.2: SyncStatus reflects CRDT sync health; unsynchronised changes are indicated visually.
  req F-8.3:
    when: a peer starts or stops attending an object
    then: viewersByObject is updated in ephemeral plugin state
  req F-8.4: Peers report and look up presence by object EID. A graph path resolves to its innermost object, or to the space's own EID when it names no object.
  req F-8.5: SpacePresence shows peers in an order that is the same on every client for a given set of peers and changes only when the set changes.
  req F-8.6: A viewer whose heartbeat has lapsed for two broadcast intervals drops out of both presence indicators.
  req F-8.7: A space's navtree row counts the peers viewing the space itself.
  req F-8.8: An object's navtree row shows the progress monitors keyed to it (`<object uri>#<suffix>`): a pulsing star while one runs, over presence, and a red edge when one fails. Each monitor's label is a line of the row's tooltip.
  req F-8.9: Each peer in a space has a hidden app-graph node whose actions act on that peer: Jump when the object the peer views is open in the deck, Go to otherwise. Go to opens the object at the graph path the peer's session has it open at, so the navtree shows it where the peer does.
  req F-8.10: Jump reveals the peer's selection, or the top of their viewport when they have none, moving the caret and taking focus.
  req F-8.11: Clicking an avatar in SpacePresence opens the list of the object's viewers with that peer's row highlighted; a button at the end of its header opens the Members companion. Rows are Listbox rows whose actions are labelled buttons.
  req F-8.12: The Members deck companion lists every online peer in the space, grouped by the object they view, with the same actions; an Invite members action at the end of its toolbar opens the space's members settings. It sits third in the complementary rail, after Notifications.
  req F-8.18: A presence row's avatar sits inside the row's hover and highlight. A person's row and their session rows hover and highlight together, as one block.
  req F-8.15: In a locked space the Members companion shows only a placeholder saying the space is private, since it has no other members and no members settings.
  req F-8.13: A peer with several sessions (tabs or devices) on an object shows as one row, whose actions act on whichever of those sessions moved its anchor most recently, never on a session attending another object; with none attending the object, the row has no actions. A toggle in the viewers list's header and in the Members companion's toolbar lists each peer's sessions under their row, each named by its device and with its own actions while it attends the object; the peer's row then carries none. A peer is never listed twice. Both lists share the toggle's state, kept per device.
  req F-8.14: The viewing message carries the sender's session id, its device, the location in each object its deck holds, and the graph paths of its deck's planks in the space with the one it is scrolled to; it is sent with the heartbeat and at most once per second when a location changes, or every 100 ms while followed ([F-8.20]).
  req F-8.16: A session row's dot shows whether its anchor moved in the last minute (active) or not (idle); the row states nothing else about the session.
  req F-8.17: A session row names its device by the label someone gave it, else by what it runs ("Chrome on macOS", "Composer on iOS"); sessions on one device are numbered. A placeholder label the SDK once wrote is no label.
  req F-8.19: A peer's node carries Follow, which follows whichever of their sessions moved most recently, switching as that changes; a session's node carries Follow for that session alone. Neither shows while it is already the followed target.
  req F-8.20: A follower names its target in its viewing message. A session that sees itself named sends location changes at most every 100 ms to the whole space, instead of every second.
  req F-8.21: While following, a follower whose deck lays planks side by side shows the leader's deck: the planks it holds in the space, in order, scrolled to the plank at its front, each revealing the top of the leader's viewport there, or their selection when they report no viewport. A follower whose deck is flat opens the object the leader attends, at the leader's path, whenever it changes, and reveals their anchor in it. Reveals go through the type's `Locator` without moving the follower's caret or focus. An object the follower cannot open pauses the follow until the leader attends one it can.
  req F-8.22: A follow ends when the follower scrolls, clicks, touches or types in any object's plank, presses Escape, attends an object outside what it shows of the leader, or leaves the space's workspace for Settings or another space; and when the leader has attended nothing in the space for five seconds, which their leaving the space, going offline or their heartbeat lapsing all amount to. The leader going idle ends nothing.
  req F-8.23: While following, the Members companion's rail tab shows a dot, and its list starts with the leader's row, highlighted, carrying Stop (and Paused while paused) in place of their actions. Stopping returns the row to its object's group and clears the dot.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Create and open a space
  given: no spaces exist
  when: op:SpaceOperation.Create runs with name "Acme"
  then:
    - new Space object is returned with the given name
    - space appears in the navigation graph
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Join space via invitation
  given: an invitation URL has been generated for an existing space
  when: op:SpaceOperation.Join runs with the invitation code
  then:
    - space appears in the local client's space list
    - space state transitions to SPACE_READY
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Add and remove object with undo
  given: a Collection in an active space
  when: op:SpaceOperation.AddObject adds object X, then op:SpaceOperation.RemoveObjects removes it
  then:
    - RemoveObjects output records the original index and collection
    - op:SpaceOperation.RestoreObjects puts X back at the same index
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Export and import space
  given: a space containing 5 objects
  when: op:SpaceOperation.ExportSpace runs, then op:SpaceOperation.ImportSpace loads the archive
  then:
    - the new space contains the same 5 objects
    - the original space is unchanged
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: Schema registration
  given: an active space with no custom schemas
  when: op:SpaceOperation.AddSchema runs with a new schema definition
  then:
    - a StoredSchema entry exists in the space database
    - the schema is available in the create-object dialog type picker
```

```mdl
scenario T-6: View field delete and restore
  given: a View with fields ["name", "email", "phone"]
  when: op:SpaceOperation.DeleteField removes "email", then op:SpaceOperation.RestoreField restores it
  then:
    - after delete, View has fields ["name", "phone"]
    - after restore, View has fields ["name", "email", "phone"] in original order
```

---

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Create a space, add and remove an object
  desc: The core space round-trip — create a space, add an object to it, remove it with undo data.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-1.1, F-3.1, T-1, T-3]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - no space named "QA Space" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the space
      do: Click "New space" in the sidebar and name it "QA Space".
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.Create] { name: "QA Space" }
      capture: created
      expect: a new space named "QA Space" exists and opens in the navtree
      assert: return $created.space.properties.name === 'QA Space';
    - name: Create a collection to add to
      do: In "QA Space", click + and choose Collection. Name it "QA Collection".
      invoke: [op:CollectionOperation.Create] { name: "QA Collection" }
      capture: collection
      expect: a Collection named "QA Collection" exists in the space
      assert: return $collection.object.name === 'QA Collection';
    - name: Add an object to the space
      do: In the navtree, click + on "QA Collection" and choose Markdown. Name it "QA Doc".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.markdown.create { name: "QA Doc" }
      capture: doc
      expect: a Document named "QA Doc" now exists
    - name: Place it in the collection
      do: (the navtree create action places it for you)
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.AddObject] { object: $doc.object, target: $collection.object }
      capture: added
      expect: "QA Doc" appears as a row under "QA Collection"
      assert: return $collection.object.objects.some((ref) => ref.target?.id === $doc.object.id);
      note: Coalesced with the previous step — `doc.object` is live and cannot cross a snippet boundary.
    - name: Remove the object
      do: Right-click "QA Doc" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.RemoveObjects] { objects: [$doc.object], target: $collection.object }
      capture: removed
      expect: "QA Doc" leaves the navtree row list under "QA Collection"
      assert: return $removed.objects.some((o) => o.id === $doc.object.id);
    - name: Restore the object
      do: Undo the delete (Cmd/Ctrl+Z), or use the undo toast.
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.RestoreObjects] { objects: $removed.objects, parentCollection: $removed.parentCollection, indices: $removed.indices, wasActive: $removed.wasActive }
      expect: "QA Doc" reappears as a row under "QA Collection"
      assert: return $collection.object.objects.some((ref) => ref.target?.id === $doc.object.id);
  after:
    - name: Delete the space
      do: Right-click "QA Space" in the sidebar and choose Delete Space.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.delete { space: $created.space }
      expect: "QA Space" no longer appears in the sidebar
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Register a schema and add a typed relation
  desc: Schema-registry and relation round-trip — the machinery plugin-table/plugin-kanban build on.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-4.1, T-5]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - no schema typename "example.org/type/QaThing" is already registered in the space — ABORT
      rather than reusing a registration this test did not create
    - schema: a runtime `Schema.Struct` for typename "example.org/type/QaThing" to register
    - relationSchema: a runtime relation schema (source/target typed) to link `a` and `b` with
    - a: an object already in the space, the relation's source
    - b: an object already in the space, the relation's target
  steps:
    - name: Register the schema
      do: Open Settings -> Schema for the space and register a new type, or create an object of a
        new type from the type picker, which registers it implicitly.
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.AddSchema] { db: $given.space.db, typename: "example.org/type/QaThing", schema: $given.schema, show: true }
      capture: registered
      expect: the type appears in the space's schema registry and in the create-object type picker
      assert: return $registered.object.typename === 'example.org/type/QaThing';
    - name: Add a typed relation between two objects
      do: With two objects selected, use the relation-creation affordance to link them with the
        registered relation schema.
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.AddRelation] { db: $given.space.db, schema: $given.relationSchema, source: $given.a, target: $given.b }
      expect: a relation now exists linking the two objects, visible wherever relations render
      assert: return !!$result.relation;
  after:
    - name: No teardown
      do: Schema registrations are not removed by this test — they are lightweight and harmless
        to leave in a scratch space.
      expect: the space still opens cleanly and the registered schemas remain listed
```

```mdl
test QA-3: Act on a peer from their avatar
  desc: A peer's avatar opens the object's viewers, Jump reveals what they are looking at, and the Members companion lists everyone in the space.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-8.9, F-8.10, F-8.11, F-8.12]
  status: unverified
  automated:
    - composer-e2e:collaboration.spec.ts#Collaboration tests › a peer's avatar opens the viewers list and jumps to their selection
  given:
    - host: a booted app with a space containing one document, shared with a guest
    - guest: a second browser profile with its own identity, a member of that space
  steps:
    - name: Both open the document
      do: Open the same document on both peers, and type a line on the guest.
      expect: the host's plank header shows the guest's avatar
    - name: Open the viewers list
      do: On the host, click the guest's avatar.
      expect: a list of the document's viewers opens with the guest's row highlighted, and a Jump action on it
    - name: Jump to the guest
      do: Click Jump on the guest's row.
      expect: the host's editor takes focus with its caret at the guest's selection
    - name: See everyone
      do: Open the viewers list again and click the members button in its header.
      expect: the Members companion opens in the complementary sidebar and lists the guest under the document
    - name: Invite more
      do: Click "Invite members" in the Members companion.
      expect: the space's members settings open
```

```mdl
test QA-4: Tell a peer's sessions apart
  desc: A peer with the object open in two tabs shows as one row, and the sessions toggle lists their sessions under it, each with its own Jump.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-8.13, F-8.16]
  status: unverified
  automated:
    - composer-e2e:collaboration.spec.ts#Collaboration tests › the sessions toggle lists a peer's sessions under their row, each with its own Jump
  given:
    - host: a booted app with a space containing one document, shared with a guest
    - guest: a second browser profile with its own identity, a member of that space
  steps:
    - name: Open the document twice
      do: Open the document on the host, and in two tabs of the guest's.
      expect: the host's plank header shows one avatar for the guest
    - name: Open the viewers list
      do: On the host, click the guest's avatar.
      expect: the guest's row carries a Jump action
    - name: Show each session
      do: Click the sessions toggle in the list's header.
      expect: a row per session appears under the guest's row, each named by its device with a dot and a Jump action, and the guest's own row no longer carries Jump
    - name: Jump to a session
      do: Click Jump on the first session's row.
      expect: the host's editor takes focus
```

```mdl
test QA-5: Follow a peer around the space
  desc: Following a peer from the Members companion opens what they open and keeps their top line in view without taking focus, marks the companion's tab, and Escape or leaving the space ends it.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-8.19, F-8.20, F-8.21, F-8.22, F-8.23]
  status: unverified
  automated:
    - composer-e2e:collaboration.spec.ts#Collaboration tests › following a peer opens what they open and mirrors their scroll until Escape or leaving the space
  given:
    - host: a booted app with a space containing two documents, shared with a guest
    - guest: a second browser profile with its own identity, a member of that space
  steps:
    - name: Both open the first document
      do: Open the first document on both peers.
      expect: the host's plank header shows the guest's avatar
    - name: Follow the guest
      do: On the host, open the Members companion and click Follow on the guest's row.
      expect: the Members tab shows a dot, and the guest's row is first and highlighted, with Stop in place of its actions
    - name: The guest opens the other document
      do: On the guest, open the second document and type enough lines to scroll it, ending at the bottom.
      expect: the host's deck opens the second document and scrolls it down with the guest's, while the host's caret and focus stay where they were
    - name: Stop with Escape
      do: On the host, press Escape.
      expect: the dot clears, and the guest's row is back under their document with Follow among its actions
    - name: Leave for Settings
      do: On the host, follow the guest again, open Settings, then return to the space.
      expect: the follow ended when the host left the space: no dot, and the guest's row has Follow among its actions
```

```mdl
test QA-6: Follow a peer's deck side by side
  desc: A follower whose deck is not flattened shows the leader's planks in the leader's order and scrolls its deck with theirs.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-8.21]
  status: unverified
  automated:
    - composer-e2e:collaboration.spec.ts#Collaboration tests › a follower whose deck lays planks side by side mirrors the leader's planks and scroll
  given:
    - host: a booted app with the deck's flatten setting off, and a space containing three documents, shared with a guest
    - guest: a second browser profile with its own identity and the flatten setting off, a member of that space
  steps:
    - name: The guest opens three planks
      do: On the guest, open the first document, then shift-click the second and third.
      expect: the guest's deck shows the three documents side by side
    - name: Follow the guest
      do: On the host, open the Members companion and click Follow on the guest's row.
      expect: the host's deck shows the same three planks, in the guest's order
    - name: The guest scrolls their deck
      do: On the guest, bring the first plank to the front, then the last.
      expect: each time, the host's deck scrolls to show the plank the guest brought to the front
    - name: Stop with Escape
      do: On the host, press Escape.
      expect: the Members tab's dot clears
```

