## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: SpacePresence shows peers in a stable order, the same for any given set of peers, that changes only when the set changes.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [SpacePresence, F-8.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Peers are ordered by hex identity key. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [SpacePresence, F-8.5]
  why: The identity key is the same on every client and does not change while a peer stays, so the order moves only when the set does.
  rejected:
    - Ordering by last-seen time, which every heartbeat refreshes and so reshuffles the avatars each interval.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Presence is keyed by object EID rather than graph path, with a path resolving to its innermost object or to its space.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.4, SpacePresence, PluginState]
  why: The sender holds graph paths and the receivers hold objects; the EID is what both resolve to. Graph paths alone matched neither receiver.
  rejected:
    - Keying by graph path, which the plank header cannot derive from the object it renders.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: A viewer expires after two missed heartbeats in both the navtree and plank-header indicators.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.6]
  why: An expiry equal to the broadcast interval let a viewer flicker out between heartbeats, and the avatars applied no expiry at all.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: Remove `viewersByIdentity` from the ephemeral state.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [PluginState, F-8.3]
  why: Nothing read it.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: A space's navtree row shows how many peers view the space, as the navbar already does.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.7, SpacePresence]
  why: Space rows render the sync-status glyph, which took no presence, so a space with viewers always showed none.
  rejected: Let the presence surface claim space rows; the navtree renders one end surface per row, so the sync status would be lost.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: When the deck switches workspace, the planks that left `active` are reported as removed.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.3]
  why: The new workspace's layout lists none of the old planks, so peers in the old space kept the viewer until its heartbeat lapsed.
  rejected: Treat an empty heartbeat as clearing the peer; heartbeats are not complete updates, so an empty one cannot be told from a partial one.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: The navtree presence surface claims space rows, which no longer carry a sync-status glyph.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-6
  affects: [F-8.7, SpacePresence]
  why: Sync status moved to the status bar, so nothing on a space row is lost when presence takes it, and space rows draw the same glyph, with the same treatments, as object rows.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: Activity on an object reaches its navtree glyph through the progress registry, not a capability of its own.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.8, SpacePresence]
  why: The progress registry is already the app's channel for work under way, keyed per object by convention; reading it means any producer (an agent turn, a mailbox sync) shows on the row without plugin-space knowing about it.
  rejected: An `ActivitySource` capability that each plugin contributes per object; a second channel for the same signal.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: Peers get Go to and Jump actions in the app graph; Jump moves the caret and takes focus, as revealing a comment does.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.9, F-8.10]
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Clicking an avatar opens the member list with its row highlighted. The list shows only that object's viewers and ends with a "See everyone in this space" button that opens a People companion in the complementary sidebar listing everyone in the space.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.11, F-8.12, SpacePresence]
```

```mdl
decision D-12: A peer on several devices shows as one row, using the latest device. The navtree presence indicators stay as they are.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.13, F-8.7]
```

```mdl
decision D-13: Each peer is a hidden graph node under its space, `peer-<identityKey>`, so actions can depend on what the peer views. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.9]
  why: Actions differ per object type and per whether the object is open, so a fixed per-member menu cannot express them.
  rejected: One static action set per member, chosen in the component.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: Jump is offered only when the peer's object is open in the deck and its type contributes a `Locator`; Go to only when it is not open. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.9, F-8.10]
  why: Offering both on an open object duplicates one outcome; Go to cannot reveal yet because the target opens after the action returns.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: Locations ride the existing `viewing` message, sent with the heartbeat and throttled to one per second on change. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.14]
  why: Jump needs only a recent location; the faster rate belongs to following, which raises it only while someone follows.
  rejected: A separate location message; two messages per peer would need their own expiry.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: The companion is named Members, matching the members settings, and links to the members settings to invite more people. In a locked space it shows a placeholder, since there are no other members and no members settings.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-11
  affects: [F-8.11, F-8.12, F-8.15]
```

```mdl
decision D-17: The invite link opens the members settings through `SpaceOperation.OpenMembers` and shows even when no one else is online; the locked placeholder replaces the whole list. Fills in [D-16].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.12, F-8.15]
  why: An empty space is when inviting matters most; a locked space can list no one but you.
```

```mdl
decision D-18: Invite members is a button at the end of the companion's toolbar. Presence rows are built on the react-ui Listbox, so spacing and keyboard navigation come from it, and their actions are visible buttons rather than ghost icons. Notifications comes second in the complementary rail and Members third.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.11, F-8.12]
```

```mdl
decision D-19: The popover opens the companion from a button at the end of its header, and labels its action "Jump"; Notifications and Members take rail positions -2 and -1. Fills in [D-18].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.11, F-8.12]
  why: A full-width footer label overflowed the popover; the header's trailing slot is where a popover's own controls go. Explicit positions keep the rail order from depending on plugin load order.
  rejected: Keep the footer button and widen the popover to fit it.
```

```mdl
decision D-20: Viewers are tracked per session (a tab or app instance), not per identity. A peer with several sessions on an object is one row that expands, behind a disclosure, into a row per session naming its device.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-12
  affects: [F-8.13, ObjectViewerProps, PluginState]
```

```mdl
decision D-21: Expanded, only the session rows carry actions. Collapsed, the peer's row carries them, acting on the peer's default session.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.13]
```

```mdl
decision D-22: The default session is the one whose anchor (selection or viewport) changed most recently, from typing, scrolling or any other move. A session is active while its anchor changed recently and idle otherwise, shown by a dot alone with no text; editing is not told apart from viewing.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.13, F-8.16]
```

```mdl
decision D-23: Each running app picks a random session id and sends it, with its device name, in every `viewing` message. The name is the HALO device profile's label, else its platform and OS, matching the devices settings. A message without a session id counts as one session keyed by the identity. Fills in [D-20].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.14, ObjectViewerProps]
  why: A peer cannot read another identity's device profiles, so the sender names its own device. Keying old clients by identity keeps them listed as one session.
  rejected: Look the device up by the gossip envelope's peer id, which only works for one's own devices.
```

```mdl
decision D-24: Receivers derive when a session moved by comparing each message's location with the one before; opening an object or coming back to it counts as a move. Active means moved within the last 60 s. Fills in [D-22].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.16, ObjectViewerProps]
  why: Locations already travel on change, so the receiver sees every move without a new field, and its own clock judges the window, so clock skew between devices does not matter.
  rejected: A sender-side `idleFor` field counting seconds since the last input.
```

```mdl
decision D-25: Each session is a hidden graph node, `session-<sessionId>`, under its peer's node and carries the same Jump and Go to actions for that session. Fills in [D-21].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.9, F-8.13]
  why: Keeps the actions in the app graph, as [D-13] does for peers, so a session's Jump depends on what that session views.
```

```mdl
decision D-26: Sessions on the same device are numbered after its name, the session count sits on a description line under the peer's name, and the caret is the row's trailing Collapsible trigger. The popover takes its 24rem maximum width. The Members companion lists a peer under each object one of their sessions attends, with only those sessions, and its collapsed row acts on the most recently moved of them. Fills in [D-20].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.11, F-8.12, F-8.13]
  why: Two tabs on one device carry the same name. The count beside the name truncated next to Jump in a 20rem popover. The trailing caret is how Listbox rows collapse elsewhere.
  rejected: A leading caret before the avatar, as first mocked.
```

```mdl
decision D-27: On a peer's row the session count follows the name as plain text, not a tag, and the caret is a separate control fixed at the row's end. Expanding the row moves nothing on it; only its Jump goes away.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.13]
```

```mdl
decision D-28: Devices get proper names in the UI. The SDK stops writing a placeholder device label, and every place that names a device treats that placeholder as no label.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.17]
```

```mdl
decision D-29: Two sessions on the same device each get their own row.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.13, F-8.17]
```

```mdl
decision D-30: Session rows sit under the peer's name: the dot in the cell under the avatar, then a device icon for its kind and the device's name, then Jump at the row's end, in line with single-session rows' Jump. The popover takes the Members companion's size (`md`) and its 24rem maximum width. Rows on one device are numbered after its name. The Members companion lists a peer under each object one of their sessions attends, with only those sessions, and its collapsed row acts on the most recently moved of them. Fills in [D-27] and [D-29].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-26
  affects: [F-8.11, F-8.12, F-8.13, F-8.17]
  why: At the plank header's `lg` size, Jump and a trailing dot left device names too little room to show their numbers; the cell under the avatar was empty.
  rejected: Keep the count on a description line under the name; keep the dot beside Jump.
```

```mdl
decision D-31: Each running app picks a random session id and sends it, with its device as label, platform, OS and kind, in every `viewing` message; a message without a session id counts as one session keyed by the identity. A shared `getDeviceLabel` in the client SDK drops the placeholders `initial identity device` and `additional device`, for the presence sender, the devices settings and the device CLI alike. The receiver names a device by its label, else "Composer on <os>" for the native and mobile apps, else "<platform> on <os>". Fills in [D-28].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-23
  affects: [F-8.14, F-8.17, SessionDevice]
  why: Devices already written with a placeholder keep it in their HALO credentials, so readers must ignore it as well as the SDK no longer writing it. Sending the parts lets the receiver localize the name and pick the icon.
  rejected: Send a preformatted name string; rename existing devices with a new profile credential.
```

```mdl
decision D-32: A toggle in the toolbar switches presence lists between a row per person and a row per session, in place of the caret that expanded a person's row; with it there is no disclosure. Replaces the disclosure of [D-20] and [D-21].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-27
  affects: [F-8.13]
```

```mdl
decision D-33: A presence row's avatar must not stick out of the row's hover background.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.18]
```

```mdl
decision D-34: The sessions toggle sits before See everyone in the viewers popover's header and at the end of the Members companion's toolbar, before Invite members. Both read one `showSessions` flag in the plugin's persisted state, so the choice holds across the two lists and reloads on this device. A person's row keeps one line with a small (`sm`) avatar and the session count after the name. A session row takes two lines, the peer's name over the dot and device name, with an `md` avatar, ordered by device name. Rows draw no status ring on the avatar, and the device-kind icon is gone. Fills in [D-32] and [D-33].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-30
  affects: [F-8.11, F-8.12, F-8.13, F-8.17, F-8.18, PluginState]
  why: An avatar a block tall fills a one-line row to its edges, and its ring's gap is painted in the surface colour, so it shows as a pale disc against the hover. On one line, a session row's name and device both truncated at the companion's width.
  rejected: A dot badge on the avatar (its ring would show the same pale disc); one-line session rows; a separate toggle state per list.
```

```mdl
decision D-35: With the sessions toggle on, a person is still one row and their sessions are listed under it; the same identity is never shown more than once. The toggle in the toolbar only picks whether the sessions are listed.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-34
  affects: [F-8.13]
```

```mdl
decision D-36: Every presence row uses the same, smaller avatar.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.18]
```

```mdl
decision D-37: A person's row keeps one line with an `sm` avatar and the session count after the name. With the toggle on, every listed person's sessions follow their row, a person with one session included, and the person's row drops its actions for theirs. A session row has the dot in the cell under the avatar and the device's name lined up with the person's name, then Jump; rows on a device are ordered by its name. Rows draw no status ring on the avatar, and there is no device-kind icon. The toggle and its persisted `showSessions` flag stay as in [D-34]. Fills in [D-35] and [D-36].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.11, F-8.12, F-8.13, F-8.17, F-8.18, PluginState]
  why: Listing single-session people's sessions too keeps the toggle's meaning the same for every row and still shows which device they are on. One-line session rows fit once the person's name is not repeated on them.
  rejected: List sessions only for people with several; keep two-line session rows with the larger avatar.
```

```mdl
decision D-38: A person's row and the session rows listed under it are one block: hovering or highlighting any of them shows the hover across all of them.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.18]
```

```mdl
decision D-39: A person's rows sit in one group that takes the hover and highlight background while any of its rows is hovered or highlighted; the rows inside paint none of their own. The keyboard's ring still marks the one row the keys act on, so the row theme rings a highlighted row nested two levels under its list as well as one. Fills in [D-38].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.18]
  why: Listbox rows cannot nest, so the person's row and its session rows stay siblings and their shared state has to come from a wrapper. In the Members companion the wrapper sits inside the object's group, one level deeper than the row theme rang.
  rejected: Highlight the person's row alone and hover each session row separately, as Listbox does by default.
```

```mdl
decision D-40: The plank header's avatars expand the graph nodes of their peers and those peers' sessions, so the viewers list's Jump and Go to are there when it opens. Expanding them only when the list rendered left the person's Jump to appear about a second later.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.11]
  why: Peer and session nodes are hidden, so nothing else expands them, and expanding a node builds its actions asynchronously.
  rejected: Reserve the Jump's space in the row while its actions load.
```

```mdl
decision D-41: A person's row does not show how many sessions they have.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.13]
```

```mdl
decision D-42: In the viewers list, a person's row acts on the most recently moved of their sessions attending that object, and has no actions when none is. It used to act on their most recently moved session anywhere in the space, so its Jump or Go to could target another object. Fills in [D-22].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.13, SpacePresence]
  why: The list is titled "In this document", so its actions must act on that document; the Members companion already picks its row's session this way.
  rejected: Fall back to the person's first session, which can attend another object.
```

```mdl
decision D-43: With the sessions toggle on, a session row in the viewers list has actions only while its session attends that object. A session that moved to another object stays listed until its heartbeat lapses. Fills in [D-42].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.13, SpacePresence]
  why: Jump and Go to on such a row would act on the other object, the case [D-42] rules out for the person's row.
  rejected: Drop such sessions from the list, which would hide that the peer still has the object open.
```

```mdl
decision D-44: The viewing message carries the sender's deck in that space as the graph paths of its planks, in order. Go to opens the peer's object at the path the peer's session has it open at, and falls back to the object's path under the space's database section when the session sent no deck.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.9, F-8.14, PeerDeck, PluginState]
  why: Presence keys name an object, not where it sits in the tree. Opening the object's database path expanded the Database section in the follower's navtree, though the peer had opened it from a collection.
  rejected: Resolve a collection that holds the object on the receiving side, which can pick a different collection than the peer's, or the wrong section entirely.
```

```mdl
decision D-45: Follow is one action among a peer's actions, next to Jump and Go to, and follows the peer across the whole space. While someone follows, the leader's location goes out every 100 ms, broadcast over gossip to the whole space, instead of every second. The follower names its leader in its own presence state, and a leader that sees itself named switches to the fast rate.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.14, F-8.19, F-8.20]
```

```mdl
decision D-46: A follower opens the object the leader attends whenever it changes and reveals the leader's anchor through the type's `Locator`. Revealing while following must not take focus or move the follower's caret. On a canvas, follow adopts the leader's zoom.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.21]
```

```mdl
decision D-47: A follow ends when the follower scrolls, types, changes selection, navigates or moves attention to another plank, or presses Escape, and when the leader goes offline, leaves the space or their location goes stale. The leader opening something the follower cannot open pauses the follow. The leader going idle ends nothing.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.21, F-8.22]
```

```mdl
decision D-48: Following shows only in the Members companion. While following, its rail tab shows a dot, and the followed person's row moves to the top of its list, highlighted, with Stop in place of its actions. Stopping puts the row back and clears the dot. The dot widens the deck companion's existing badge rather than adding another.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.23]
```

```mdl
decision D-49: Follow on a person's row follows whichever of their sessions moved most recently, switching as that changes, as Jump does. With the sessions toggle on, each session row has its own Follow, which stays on that session.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.19, FollowTarget]
```

```mdl
decision D-50: The follower's input ends a follow when it is a pointer press, wheel, touch move or key press inside an element whose attendable id names an object, which covers its planks and their companions; a modifier key alone does not count. Escape ends it from anywhere, and attending an object other than the leader's counts as navigating. A leader whose sessions have attended nothing in the space for five seconds has left, gone offline or gone stale, which also catches their heartbeat lapsing. Fills in [D-47].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.22]
  why: Input events read the same for every object type, so no view has to tell its own reveal scrolls apart from the user's, and a scroll the app makes fires no wheel or key event. Five seconds absorbs the gap between a leader leaving one object and attending the next.
  rejected:
    - End on any change to the followed view's reported viewport that the view did not tag as a reveal; every view would need to tag reveals, and the scroll events of a reveal arrive after its transaction.
    - End the moment the leader attends nothing, which a plank switch does briefly.
```

```mdl
decision D-51: A `Locator`'s reveal takes a `follow` flag. With it, markdown scrolls the anchor to the top of the view and leaves the selection and focus alone, and a sheet scrolls the anchor's cell to the top left without moving its focused cell. The follower reveals the top of the leader's viewport, else their selection, and for five seconds after opening an object reveals again every half second so a view that mounts late still lands. No canvas has a `Locator` yet, so adopting the leader's zoom waits for one. Fills in [D-46].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.21]
  why: The viewport anchor shows what the leader sees, where the caret may be off screen. A flag keeps one reveal per type for comments, Jump and follow.
  rejected: A second reveal operation per type for following.
```

```mdl
decision D-52: The follower names `{ identityKey, sessionId? }` in its viewing messages to the leader's space only. The leader keeps its followers by space, identity and session, drops one whose message stops naming it or whose heartbeat lapses, and sends at once when a new one appears so the follower starts from a fresh location. The markdown editor reports its location every 100 ms instead of 250 ms, so the fast rate has moves to send. Fills in [D-45].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.14, F-8.20]
  why: Naming the leader in the space it is followed in keeps other spaces' leaders at the slow rate. At 250 ms the editor would cap the fast tier at a quarter second.
  rejected: A separate presence channel for followers.
```

```mdl
decision D-53: Follow is left off the node that is already the followed target. The leader's row at the top of the Members companion lists no sessions even with the toggle on, and reads Paused before Stop while the follow is paused. The companion `badge` atom holds `number | true`, and `true` draws a dot with no text. Fills in [D-48] and [D-49].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.19, F-8.23, PluginState]
  why: A Follow for the current target would do nothing. With Stop on the person's row, session rows under it would offer a second way to change the same follow.
  rejected: Turn Follow into Stop on the followed node, which would put a second Stop in the viewers popover.
```

```mdl
decision D-54: A person's group of rows also takes the highlight background while one of its rows is the list's selected value, which is how the viewers list marks the clicked peer and the Members companion marks the leader. Fills in [D-39] and [D-48].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.11, F-8.18, F-8.23]
  why: The list's value sets `aria-selected` on the row, not `data-highlighted`, and the group made its rows transparent, so neither row showed as highlighted.
  rejected: Move the keyboard highlight to the row instead, which the next arrow key would move away.
```

```mdl
decision D-55: Following mirrors the leader's whole deck: the planks it holds, how far it is scrolled, and the scroll within each plank. A follower whose own deck is flat navigates by the plank the leader attends.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.21]
```

```mdl
decision D-56: The deck's scroll travels as its front plank, the first one not folded with at least half its width in view; a flat deck's front is its current plank. The follower switches to the space's workspace, sets its deck to the leader's planks, and scrolls the front plank to just past its own left pile without focusing it. Every plank's location goes out, not only the attended one's, and each mirrored plank reveals its own. A follower deck wider than the leader's can show more planks, so its own front plank may differ; it shows the leader's. For five seconds after its deck changes the follower sends the scroll and the reveals again on every tick. Attending any plank of the mirrored deck keeps the follow. A leader that sent no deck is followed as a flat deck follows. Stopping leaves the follower's deck as it is. Fills in [D-55].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.14, F-8.21, F-8.22, ObjectViewerProps, PeerDeck, QA-6]
  why: A plank, unlike a scroll offset, means the same thing in a viewport of another width. The deck moves attention to a visible plank when the attended one folds, so a scroll the follow makes can move attention inside the mirrored deck.
  rejected:
    - Send the deck's scroll offset in pixels, which lands elsewhere in a deck of another width or with other plank sizes.
    - Restore the follower's own planks when the follow stops; each mirrored deck is a browser history entry, so Back walks back to them.
```

```mdl
decision D-57: Any navigation by the follower ends the follow, including switching to Settings or another space. Fills in [D-47].
  date: 2026-11-05
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.22, QA-5]
  why: A follow that survives the follower's own navigation pulls them back on the leader's next move, the jumpy behaviour following is meant to avoid. Follow elsewhere works the same way.
  rejected:
    - Pause while the follower is away and resume when they come back to the space.
    - Keep following and bring the follower back to the space on the leader's next move.
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap
    literals?: UnionList
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap
    state?: FieldMap
    slots?: FieldMap
    actions?: ActionMap
    emits?: EventMap
    layout?: CodeBlock
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap
    output?: TypeExpr
    errors?: ErrorMap
    effects?: EffectList
    requires?: ServiceList
    note?: Prose
```
